IMPORT prelude

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition,
-- informal consolidation in force from 1 December 2025.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/SSSA2015.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill and
-- nothing else: no pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. Observations, not checked findings.
--
-- SCOPE. ss 6, 7, 10, 11 and 12 -- who is an eligible individual, including the
-- four deeming rules about attaining 65; what they are eligible for; when money
-- is recoverable as a debt; and the offence of obtaining a benefit dishonestly.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 1-5 (purpose, administration, establishment of the Scheme),
-- ss 8-9 (access to means information), ss 13-20 (certificates, powers to
-- obtain information, obstruction, bodies corporate, composition, prosecutions,
-- immunity, regulations). Those constitute and empower; they decide nothing
-- about an individual.
--
-- NO daydate. The `l4` on this machine imports `prelude` but not `daydate`, so
-- there is no DATE type here. A date is carried as its three components and
-- compared as a single ordered number, which is enough for s 6(2) because every
-- rule in it is about calendar components rather than elapsed time.

§ `Silver Support Scheme Act 2015`

§§ `6 -- Who is an eligible individual?`

-- s 6(2)(c): "where the day of the month in which an individual was born cannot
-- be ascertained, that individual is deemed to be born on the first day of that
-- month";
-- s 6(2)(d): "where the month in which an individual was born cannot be
-- ascertained, that individual is deemed to be born in January."
--
-- Both are about a fact that cannot be ascertained, so each component is MAYBE
-- and the absence is what triggers the deeming. The year is not deemed: the Act
-- assumes it is always known.
DECLARE BirthRecord HAS
    `year of birth`     IS A NUMBER
    `month of birth`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `day of birth`      IS A MAYBE NUMBER

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deemed month of birth` IS
    CONSIDER `the birth`'s `month of birth`
    WHEN JUST `the month` THEN `the month`
    OTHERWISE 1                      -- s 6(2)(d): deemed born in January

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the deemed day of birth` IS
    CONSIDER `the birth`'s `day of birth`
    WHEN JUST `the day` THEN `the day`
    OTHERWISE 1                      -- s 6(2)(c): deemed born on the first day

-- s 6(2)(a): "an individual attains 65 years of age on the 65th anniversary of
-- the date of that individual's birth";
-- s 6(2)(b): "where an individual was born on 29 February, the 65th anniversary
-- of the date of that individual's birth is deemed to occur on 1 March."
--
-- (b) is applied to the DEEMED date, not the recorded one. That matters only in
-- the case the Act does not address -- see the note at the foot of this file.
GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deemed date of birth is 29 February` IF
        `the deemed month of birth` `the birth` EQUALS 2
    AND `the deemed day of birth` `the birth` EQUALS 29

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the month of the 65th anniversary` IS
    IF   `the deemed date of birth is 29 February` `the birth`
    THEN 3                                            -- s 6(2)(b): 1 March
    ELSE `the deemed month of birth` `the birth`

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the day of the 65th anniversary` IS
    IF   `the deemed date of birth is 29 February` `the birth`
    THEN 1                                            -- s 6(2)(b): 1 March
    ELSE `the deemed day of birth` `the birth`

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the year of the 65th anniversary` IS
    `the birth`'s `year of birth` PLUS 65

-- A calendar date as one ordered number, so that "on or after" is a single
-- comparison. yyyymmdd, which orders correctly because each component is
-- bounded.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `the month` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the date as an ordered number` IS
    (`the year` TIMES 10000) PLUS (`the month` TIMES 100) PLUS `the day`

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 65th anniversary as an ordered number` IS
    `the date as an ordered number`
        (`the year of the 65th anniversary` `the birth`)
        (`the month of the 65th anniversary` `the birth`)
        (`the day of the 65th anniversary` `the birth`)

-- The individual, and the day the question is asked on.
DECLARE Individual HAS
    `name`                          IS A STRING
    `a citizen of Singapore`        IS A BOOLEAN       -- s 6(1)(a)
    `birth`                         IS A BirthRecord   -- s 6(1)(b)
    -- s 6(1)(c): "satisfies all other eligibility criteria that may be
    -- prescribed". The criteria are in regulations that were not retrieved, so
    -- this is a fact supplied -- and it is the fact that does most of the real
    -- work, see the note below.
    `satisfies all other prescribed eligibility criteria` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE AssessmentDay HAS
    `year`  IS A NUMBER
    `month` IS A NUMBER
    `day`   IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the assessment day as an ordered number` IS
    `the date as an ordered number` (`the day`'s `year`) (`the day`'s `month`) (`the day`'s `day`)

-- s 6(2)(a): attainment is ON the anniversary, so the anniversary day itself
-- counts.
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual has attained 65 years of age` IF
        `the assessment day as an ordered number` `the day`
    AT LEAST `the 65th anniversary as an ordered number` (`the individual`'s `birth`)

-- s 6(1): "an eligible individual is an individual who -- (a) is a citizen of
-- Singapore; (b) has attained 65 years of age; and (c) satisfies all other
-- eligibility criteria that may be prescribed."
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is an eligible individual` IF
        `the individual`'s `a citizen of Singapore`
    AND `the individual has attained 65 years of age` `the individual` `the day`
    AND `the individual`'s `satisfies all other prescribed eligibility criteria`

§§ `7 -- Benefits`

-- s 7(1): "An eligible individual is eligible to receive such benefits in such
-- manner and of such amounts as may be prescribed."
-- s 7(2): different benefits and amounts may be prescribed for different
-- classes of eligible individuals.
--
-- There is no amount in the Act. Everything about what is actually received is
-- prescribed, so the only question s 7 decides is the one below, and the amount
-- is a fact.
GIVEN `the individual` IS AN Individual, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is eligible to receive benefits under section 7` IF
    `the individual is an eligible individual` `the individual` `the day`

§§ `10 -- Recovery of sums overpaid`

-- s 10(1): "If any benefit under the Scheme is disbursed as a cash grant, and --
--   (a) the recipient -- (i) is not an eligible individual; or (ii) is an
--       eligible individual, but is not eligible for that cash grant; or
--   (b) the amount paid is in excess of the amount the recipient is eligible to
--       receive by way of that cash grant,
-- the amount paid or paid in excess (as the case may be) is recoverable from
-- the recipient as a debt due to the Government."
DECLARE Disbursement HAS
    `the recipient`                     IS AN Individual
    `disbursed as a cash grant`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount paid`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive`  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 10(1)(a)(ii): eligible as an individual, but not for THIS grant. A
    -- separate question from eligibility under s 6, and prescribed.
    `eligible for this particular cash grant` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10(2)(a)-(b)
    `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10(1)(a) applies` IF
        NOT `the individual is an eligible individual` (`the disbursement`'s `the recipient`) `the day`
    OR  NOT `the disbursement`'s `eligible for this particular cash grant`

GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10(1)(b) applies` IF
    `the disbursement`'s `the amount paid`
        GREATER THAN `the disbursement`'s `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive`

GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an amount is recoverable under section 10(1)` IF
        `the disbursement`'s `disbursed as a cash grant`
    AND `either limb of section 10(1) applies` `the disbursement` `the day`

GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `either limb of section 10(1) applies` IF
        `section 10(1)(a) applies` `the disbursement` `the day`
    OR  `section 10(1)(b) applies` `the disbursement`

-- "the amount paid or paid in excess (as the case may be)". Where (a) applies
-- the whole payment goes back; where only (b) applies, the excess does.
GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement, `the day` IS AN AssessmentDay
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount recoverable under section 10(1)` IS
    IF   `section 10(1)(a) applies` `the disbursement` `the day`
    THEN `the disbursement`'s `the amount paid`
    ELSE `the disbursement`'s `the amount paid`
             MINUS `the disbursement`'s `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive`

-- s 10(2): recovery where the benefit was obtained by a false statement or a
-- false document. Note "whether or not an eligible individual" -- this limb does
-- not care about s 6 at all, and it recovers the WHOLE amount obtained.
GIVEN `the disbursement` IS A Disbursement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an amount is recoverable under section 10(2)` IF
        `the disbursement`'s `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement`
    OR  `the disbursement`'s `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular`

§§ `11 -- Obtaining benefit through false or misleading statements`

-- s 11(1): "A person -- (a) who -- (i) knowingly or recklessly makes any false
-- or misleading statement; or (ii) produces or provides ... any document which
-- the person knows, or ought reasonably to know, is false in a material
-- particular; and (b) who, with the intention of dishonestly inducing another
-- person to accept the statement or document as genuine, dishonestly obtains
-- any cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme, shall be guilty of an
-- offence ..."
--
-- Limb (a) is a disjunction, limb (b) is a conjunction with it, and (b) carries
-- TWO mental elements of its own: the intention to induce, and dishonest
-- obtaining.
DECLARE AllegedOffence HAS
    `knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(i)
    `produced or provided a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(ii)
    `acted with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `dishonestly obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)

GIVEN `the allegation` IS AN AllegedOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (a) of section 11(1) is made out` IF
        `the allegation`'s `knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement`
    OR  `the allegation`'s `produced or provided a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular`

GIVEN `the allegation` IS AN AllegedOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph (b) of section 11(1) is made out` IF
        `the allegation`'s `acted with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine`
    AND `the allegation`'s `dishonestly obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme`

GIVEN `the allegation` IS AN AllegedOffence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is guilty of an offence under section 11` IF
        `paragraph (a) of section 11(1) is made out` `the allegation`
    AND `paragraph (b) of section 11(1) is made out` `the allegation`

-- s 11(1): "liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both." Maxima, so the
-- encoding states the ceiling and decides nothing about sentence.
`the maximum fine under section 11 in dollars` MEANS 5000
`the maximum imprisonment under section 11 in months` MEANS 12

§§ `12 -- Recovery of cash grant upon conviction`

-- s 12: "Where -- (a) a person has received any cash grant or other benefit ...
-- and (b) the person is convicted of an offence under this Act in connection
-- with the cash grant or other benefit, the court ... MAY, in addition to
-- imposing any penalty ..., order that the person pay ... the amount certified
-- by the administrator to be recoverable".
--
-- "may", so this is a power, not a duty. The rule says when the power arises.
GIVEN `the received a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `the convicted in connection with it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make a section 12 order` IF
        `the received a benefit`
    AND `the convicted in connection with it`
